# Local S3 test config. Copy to `.env.test` (gitignored) and edit.
# Non-secret only — credentials come from your ~/.aws profile, never from here.
#
# Loaded with Node's --env-file, which does NOT override a variable already set
# in your shell: an exported AWS_PROFILE beats the one below. s3cab's startup
# line says which it used — "Using AWS profile: X (from your environment)".

AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_PROFILE=your-profile   # uncomment for a non-default ~/.aws profile

# One bucket per tier. Each suite hard-fails without its variable, and refuses a
# name that doesn't end in the matching suffix. How to provision them:
# docs/integration-testing.md, "Create a bucket".
#
# integration is shareable — the tests assert only on their own objects.
# conformance and crash are versioned, sole-owner, and WIPED as they run, so
# never point either at a bucket anything else uses.
S3CAB_TEST_BUCKET=test-s3cab-yourname-integration           # test:integration
# S3CAB_CONFORMANCE_BUCKET=test-s3cab-yourname-conformance  # test:conformance
# S3CAB_CRASH_BUCKET=test-s3cab-yourname-crash              # test:crash

# Verbose output (full error causes) while debugging a failing test:
# S3CAB_DEBUG=1

# Point the suite at a non-AWS S3-compatible provider (Cloudflare R2, Backblaze
# B2, …); credentials still come from the AWS_* vars / your ~/.aws profile:
# AWS_ENDPOINT_URL_S3=https://your-endpoint
